ul after seeing all five cards with a reasonable two-pair hand\n- **All-in (-2):** Extremely risky and unnecessary\n\nReason:\n\nGiven that we've reached the river with both players checking through three streets post-flop, and I hold two pair (Queens and Sixes), checking is the optimal play. The opponent showed pre-flop aggression but then became passive, which could indicate they have a hand like AK (one pair) or a missed draw. Betting here would turn my hand into a bluff against better hands and might only get called by hands that beat me. My two pair has showdown value, and checking allows me to realize that value without risking additional chips in a marginal spot.\n\nAnswer: 0"}
